OK, so I've managed to get chickenpox from somewhere and one of the
effects of this is that my ability to sleep has gone out the window. Most
annoying - I've found the best way is to sleep in a chair. Anyway, whilst
trying to fall asleep, I found myself thinking "An AoRS would be rather
handy about now". From there I went on to thinking about useful in-game
uses for the AoRS, and AoS, and couldn't really think of any. Hence this: 

If you throw an amulet at an applicable monster, it has a 21-n^2 percent
chance of going around the neck of the monster, where n is the number of
squares away from the monster you are. 

An applicable monster is one that could wear the amulet anyway - anything
with a neck, AFAIK. I picked my formula because I think that if I were
standing next to someone, about 1 in 5 times I could get it on them, but
that's going to fall away quickly - exponentially, in fact. Once around
the neck, it works in the same way that it would had they put it on. 

